<h2>2. Data Science and Data Analytics</h2>
<p>Data is the new oil, but raw data is useless without the expertise to extract meaningful insights from it. Data Science engineering involves using scientific methods, processes, algorithms, and systems to extract knowledge and insights from structured and unstructured data.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>What you study:</strong> Big Data technologies (Hadoop, Spark), statistical modeling, data visualization tools (Tableau, PowerBI), R and Python, and database management.</li>
<li><strong>Career Roles:</strong> Data Scientist, Data Analyst, Business Intelligence Engineer, Big Data Engineer.</li>
<li><strong>Placement Potential:</strong> Very high. Every sector—including finance, healthcare, e-commerce, and sports—relies on data to make business decisions, creating a massive, industry-agnostic demand for data scientists.</li>
</ul>
<h2>3. Cyber Security and Blockchain Technology</h2>
<p>As the world becomes increasingly digital, the threat of cyberattacks has multiplied exponentially. Companies, governments, and financial institutions are investing billions of dollars to protect their digital infrastructure. Alongside this, Blockchain technology is revolutionizing data integrity and decentralized finance.</p>
<ul>
